# Spring Ecommerce Architecture

REST API for ecommerce with JWT auth. Base package: `com.springecommerce`.

## Stack

- Spring Boot 4.1, Java 17, Maven, Lombok
- Web MVC + Spring Data JPA + PostgreSQL
- Spring Security + JWT (`jjwt`) with roles `CUSTOMER`, `ADMIN`
- Jakarta Validation

## Package layout (layered)

```
config/
controller/
dto/
entity/
exception/
repository/
security/
service/
```

Place types in these global layer packages (not feature packages).

## API & IDs

- Auth endpoints under `/api/auth/**` (public)
- All other endpoints require authentication
- Entity IDs are Long (auto-generated)
- Unique email enforced at DB and application layer

## Auth conventions

- Register: `POST /api/auth/register` → `201 Created`
- New users get role `CUSTOMER`
- Passwords: BCrypt; never return in responses
- Emails: required, valid format, unique, stored lowercase
- JWT subject = email; include `role` claim
- Stateless session; CSRF disabled for the API

## Security & DTOs

- Constructor injection only
- Do not return JPA entities from controllers — use DTOs
- Centralized `@RestControllerAdvice` for API errors
